WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.237
Learn to tell the time in hours and minutes in analogue and digital watches including

00:00:05.237 --> 00:00:10.275
24-hour clocks and use clock to measure time to complete simple events in minutes and

00:00:10.275 --> 00:00:10.611
seconds

00:00:11.450 --> 00:00:18.446
Write 12:00 in 24-hour time if it is in the afternoon. The answer is 12:00. For PM

00:00:18.446 --> 00:00:21.327
hours 1–11, add 12 to the hour.

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:28.414
A lesson begins at 2:15 PM. What time is that on a 24-hour clock? Pause and solve it

00:00:28.414 --> 00:00:29.795
in your exercise book.

00:00:30.617 --> 00:00:35.801
The answer is 14:15. Add 12 to the PM hour for 1–11 PM.
